# Service descriptions

```elixir
Mix.install(rudof_elixir: [path: Path.expand("../..", __DIR__)], kino: "== 0.19.0")
```

## Introduction

This document contains a short introduction to [RDF](https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf11-primer/) using [rudof](https://rudof-project.github.io/). This chapter focuses on SPARQL service descriptions and [VoID](https://www.w3.org/TR/void/) metadata.

## Preliminaries: Install and configure rudof

The library is available as `rudof_elixir` from this checkout. The main entry point is the `Rudof.Session` module, through which most of the functionality is provided. Pass a TOML string to `Session.new!/1` to customize the session.

```elixir
alias Rudof.Session
import ExUnit.Assertions
rudof = Session.new!()
```


## Obtaining information about SPARQL endpoints

### When the SPARQL endpoint directly generates the service description in RDF (Uniprot)

<!-- livebook:{"break_markdown":true} -->
It is possible to get information from SPARQL endpoints that publish [service descriptions](https://www.w3.org/TR/sparql11-service-description/) using the [VoID](https://www.w3.org/TR/void/) vocabulary.

This example fetches UniProt's service description over the network, as the upstream notebook does. `Session.load_service_description/3` delegates URL loading and RDF parsing to Rust.


```elixir
service_url = "https://sparql.uniprot.org/sparql"
:ok = Session.load_service_description(rudof, {:url, service_url}, format: :turtle, reader_mode: :strict)
```

Now we can serialize the service description in JSON, for example, as:

The native API returns JSON text; `JSON.decode!/1` makes it convenient to inspect selected fields in Elixir.


```elixir
{:ok, json} = Session.serialize_service_description(rudof)
service = JSON.decode!(json)
Map.take(service, ["endpoint", "supported_language", "result_format"])
```

We also support the conversion from service descriptions to MIE format files:

The native API returns MIE JSON text here; Elixir only decodes and displays it.


```elixir
{:ok, json} = Session.serialize_service_description(rudof, :mie)
mie = JSON.decode!(json)
assert mie["schema_info"]["endpoint"] == service["endpoint"]
mie
```

## Additional Elixir examples

These checks extend the original lesson using the wrapper’s native API.


```elixir
:ok = Session.reset(rudof, :service_description)
{:error, %Rudof.Error{kind: :data_error}} = Session.serialize_service_description(rudof)
```

## Close the session

Release the native state when finished. To revisit earlier cells, evaluate from the beginning.


```elixir
:ok = Session.close(rudof)
```
